{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528569929,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23ce5470011NSt5kndX22WFz","sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","messageID":"msg_1d23cb120001b8gW5oSx5F2uVc","type":"tool","id":"call_ab177e6fed0842bfb54b3153","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n ';' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"95:| `sk-skill-convert.cjs` | Plans, and on request applies, the conversion of one skill. `plan` reads, refuses and prints every step, `apply` prints the same plan and writes only with `--apply`, and `preserve --snapshot <dir>` proves a reshaped body kept every original line. An older Skilled skill converts in place, with its machine router moved verbatim into a new sibling `ROUTER.md`. A plain skill reached through a path outside the skills root is staged under its frontmatter name and becomes a class S standalone root, and it converts only once the operator approves at least eight intent phrases, which become its `intent_signals`. A skill of neither shape is out of scope. Preflight refuses a hub declaration, a nested packet tree, a `local-` or `agent-` prefixed name, a name collision and a description over 130 characters. A skill that declares no `allowed-tools` field prints `allowed-tools: approval required; propose [...]` in its plan, and the apply writes no grant until a list is passed. A field declared twice is refused as `ALLOWED_TOOLS_DUPLICATE` rather than merged. The plain path keeps its agent output, its preservation snapshot and its staging copy in one scratch root beside the backup at `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/scratch/`, deleted when a question is declined and once the run has reported. A skill whose router already lives in `ROUTER.md` gets its frontmatter normalized and nothing else. Every write is preceded by a backup under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/`, `ROUTER.md` is created exclusively, and a parsed router that would change restores the backup. After both format gates it runs the integration rows: the advisor scan, the compiled skill graph, the reach probe with the budget row, the regression cases and the changelog file and link. |\n226:| `sk-code-quality-config.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only; `status` starts the runner's `--explain` once per batch of up to 500 sampled paths and no configured check. `init` is a dry run until `--apply`, which creates only `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` and refuses with `CONFIG_EXISTS` when that file exists. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"95:| `sk-skill-convert.cjs` | Plans, and on request applies, the conversion of one skill. `plan` reads, refuses and prints every step, `apply` prints the same plan and writes only with `--apply`, and `preserve --snapshot <dir>` proves a reshaped body kept every original line. An older Skilled skill converts in place, with its machine router moved verbatim into a new sibling `ROUTER.md`. A plain skill reached through a path outside the skills root is staged under its frontmatter name and becomes a class S standalone root, and it converts only once the operator approves at least eight intent phrases, which become its `intent_signals`. A skill of neither shape is out of scope. Preflight refuses a hub declaration, a nested packet tree, a `local-` or `agent-` prefixed name, a name collision and a description over 130 characters. A skill that declares no `allowed-tools` field prints `allowed-tools: approval required; propose [...]` in its plan, and the apply writes no grant until a list is passed. A field declared twice is refused as `ALLOWED_TOOLS_DUPLICATE` rather than merged. The plain path keeps its agent output, its preservation snapshot and its staging copy in one scratch root beside the backup at `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/scratch/`, deleted when a question is declined and once the run has reported. A skill whose router already lives in `ROUTER.md` gets its frontmatter normalized and nothing else. Every write is preceded by a backup under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/`, `ROUTER.md` is created exclusively, and a parsed router that would change restores the backup. After both format gates it runs the integration rows: the advisor scan, the compiled skill graph, the reach probe with the budget row, the regression cases and the changelog file and link. |\n226:| `sk-code-quality-config.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only; `status` starts the runner's `--explain` once per batch of up to 500 sampled paths and no configured check. `init` is a dry run until `--apply`, which creates only `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` and refuses with `CONFIG_EXISTS` when that file exists. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n ';' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528568647,"end":1794528569929}}}}
