{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528585308,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23d17a5001wUGOpjmpGTuFkq","sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","messageID":"msg_1d23d1120001oNNumNeVtMKXqu","type":"tool","id":"call_dfd08dc5aaf04c389fb93a23","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"| `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\n| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |","oldString":"| `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown"},"output":"Edited .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown","patch":"Index: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n+++ .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n@@ -107,8 +107,10 @@\n | `git-setup-check.cjs` | Runs the read-only sk-git setup battery for `/doctor:git setup`: eleven checks, each PASS, FAIL, SKIP, UNKNOWN or DEGRADED with the source it read and one repair per failure. It exits 0 when every check passes or skips, 3 when none failed but a check is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, 1 on any failure and 2 on a usage error. It loads every helper from its own install root and never runs code from the repository it inspects. |\n | `command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs` | Compares every command catalog and hub metadata entry back to the command's own frontmatter, which is the one copy nothing else derives from. Structural drift fails. Prose divergence reports and fails only under `--strict`. `--check` is accepted and ignored, because it is read-only either way. |\n | `doctor-helper-match.cjs` | Ranks the doctor commands of `_routes.yaml` against a problem stated in plain words for `/doctor:helper`: one entry per route, standalone command, standalone action and mcp sub-action, scored by inverse-document-frequency overlap over the manifest phrases plus a bonus for a fully covered phrase, with a preference for the mutation class the operator asked for. Each candidate carries the manifest phrase that best matched and the terms it matched, so the reason on every line is evidence. It skips its own route and every private name, reads one YAML file and writes nothing. It exits 0 on a match, 1 on no candidate above the floor and 2 on a bad argument, an unreadable manifest or a missing YAML parser. |\n | `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\n+| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n+| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | Checks this repository's OpenCode plugins on OpenCode 1 and 2. On 1 it proves plugin discovery through `debug config` and plugin load through an import check. On 2 it starts and stops a private server with the v2 binary it selected (`$OPENCODE_BIN`, `opencode` or `opencode2`, whichever reports a v2 version) and reads plugin and skill state from it. It exits 0 when every requested leg passes, 1 on a failed leg, 2 on a usage error, a crash or an `--out` file it cannot write and 3 when a leg is degraded or skipped. |\n | `ci-report.cjs` | The `/doctor:ci report` entry, kept thin: the flags, the exit codes and every name `/doctor:ci toggle` reads live here, and the readings live in the `ci-report` modules under `lib/`. It reads every workflow under `.github/workflows/` and reports its switch state, triggers, path filters and drift flags for `/doctor:ci report`. A switch is any variable a job's `if:` compares against `off`, so the workflow file is its only copy, and a repository variable value is reduced to a state and never printed. The branch, the required switch, the exempt files, the README and the rebuild trailer come from the CI profile, and the JSON names the profile it read. It exits 0 on a printed report, 1 when a workflow fails to parse, 2 on a bad argument and 3 when the CI profile is missing or invalid. |\n | `ci-scaffold.cjs` | Renders the sk-code-ci workflow or job template from the CI profile for `/doctor:ci scaffold`, and with `--protected` prints the profile's protected workflow names. It writes nothing. |\n | `ci-toggle.cjs` | Plans one switch change for `/doctor:ci toggle`: the allowlist, the refusals from the live ruleset, `neverOff` and the README, the no-op check, the exact `gh variable` command and the second named confirmation for a protected workflow. It never changes a variable. |\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"| `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\\n| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | The read-only Codex approval check: it finds the advisor's `UserPromptSubmit` entry in `.codex/hooks.json` and reports whether the Codex config holds a `trusted_hash` for that exact group and index, because Codex skips an unapproved entry without a warning. `--root <dir>` reads another checkout, `--config <path>` reads another config and `--json` prints one object. It prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks`, `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` with the `/hooks` repair line, and never prints a hash. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\\n| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | The read-only hook-wiring check: it reads `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, and reports whether the prompt hook entry is present for each runtime folder it finds. `--root <dir>` is required and `--json` prints one object. It prints `ok <runtime>` or `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, skips a runtime whose folder is absent and never writes. It exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |\",\"oldString\":\"| `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` | Scores every activated doctor phrase and each runnable doctor command through the built advisor scorer, then keeps the three results the hooks show. It fails when a phrase reaches neither the top pick nor the second line. It also fails if a runnable command does not rank first or an activated phrase has fewer than three words. It exits 2 when the advisor build is missing or stale. |\\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528581541,"end":1794528585308}}}}
