{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528590530,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23d31af002f74Z8YrYB3S1tp","sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","messageID":"msg_1d23d2a0e0017bQDCPH0dOhFGD","type":"tool","id":"call_6f814a3cae034982985ee4d2","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |","oldString":"| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown"},"output":"Edited .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown","patch":"Index: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n+++ .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n@@ -230,8 +230,10 @@\n | `sk-code-quality-config.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only; `status` starts the runner's `--explain` once per batch of up to 500 sampled paths and no configured check. `init` is a dry run until `--apply`, which creates only `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` and refuses with `CONFIG_EXISTS` when that file exists. |\n | `agents-md-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root: it reads the instruction file, its runtime copies and `REPO RULES.md`, runs three owner tools as children in their check-only forms and writes nothing. |\n | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n | `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n+| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n+| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\n | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | The battery itself writes only the `--out` file and temporary folders it removes when each step ends. The private server's folder is also removed on `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, and the server is stopped. The import check runs each plugin's v1 factory in a child process rooted at the repository, so anything a plugin does when it loads happens during the check. It never touches the shared v2 service and never prints the private server's password. OpenCode 1 writes into a temporary data folder, not the user's. |\n \n Do not invoke a mutating path from a route classified as read-only.\n \n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\\n| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\\n| `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. |\\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |\",\"oldString\":\"| `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\\n| `opencode-version-battery.cjs` |\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528588207,"end":1794528590530}}}}
