{"type":"text","timestamp":1794528610303,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","part":{"id":"prt_1d23d7df4002EyzPwfcVqBje9I","sessionID":"ses_e2dc43bf5ffeX6kMjGW052ltCf","messageID":"msg_1d23d6b1c001FC3YbL1UkmGEU1","type":"text","text":"T018 is done. The two doctor scripts are now documented in all three places in `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown`.\n\n**File written**\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown`, and no other file.\n\n**What changed**\n- Directory tree: added `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` after `ci-toggle.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` after `git-standards.cjs`.\n- Section 3 key-files table: one row per script with its flags and exit codes.\n- Section 6 read-only table: one row per script stating the read-only boundary and exit codes.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"codex-hook-approval-check.cjs|hook-wiring-check.cjs\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\n6\n$ echo $?\n0\n```\n\n6 exceeds the required 4. Exit status read as 0.\n\n**Flags and exit codes sourced from the scripts themselves**, read before writing: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` takes `--root <dir>`, `--config <path>`, `--json` and exits 0 on skip or approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry, 2 on a bad argument. `hook-wiring-check.cjs` takes required `--root <dir>` and optional `--json`, and exits 0 when every installed runtime is wired, 1 when one is missing, 2 on a bad argument or a missing root.\n\n`git status` for the file reads ` M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown`. The T018 checkbox was left unticked as instructed. Nothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794528607732,"end":1794528610303}}}
